// A 2/2 vanilla carrying ONLY Ward {2} ([CR#702.21a]) — "Whenever this
// permanent becomes the target of a spell or ability an opponent controls,
// counter it unless that player pays {2}." No card in the canon corpus has
// Ward, so this minimal carrier isolates the keyword's trigger RESOLUTION: the
// targeting spell binds as `EventObject` (the event-provenance the engine
// derives for a `BecameTarget` fact), so the collapsed `May(Pay(cost))` toll
// bills that spell's controller ([CR#702.21a] "that player") and
// `Counter(EventObject)` counters the spell on the stack, not the warded
// permanent.
Normal(
    name: "Ward Creature",
    mana_cost: [Generic(1), Blue],
    types: [Creature],
    power: 2,
    toughness: 2,
    abilities: [Keyword(Ward(cost: [Mana([Generic(2)])]))],
)
